      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Scientific research in this area typically uses broad, validated psychological scales rather than creating ad-hoc questions based on stereotypes. Instead of direct behavioral indicators, researchers often investigate variables like chronic stress levels, perceived social support, or community cohesion. These objective measures help examine how environmental pressures impact mental health and behavior without relying on biased assumptions about specific demographics. Focusing on measurable stressors provides a more rigorous and ethical framework for your sociological analysis.",
